Z||000008||FieroJoe||03-05-2001||05:01 PM||||Alright, that is the muffler that I need then!  Would I just have to take off the old mounting thingys and weld them to the new flowmaster?  and, isnt there an offset inlet or outlet pipe?<P>Second question:  I was planning on keeping stock tips, and taking out the cat.  The car has 220,000 miles on it, and I think the cat is probably overdue to either be replaced or eliminated.  should I:<P>1.  No cat/flowmaster/stock tips<BR>2.  Rodney's cat/flowmaster/stock tips<BR>3.  Rodney's cat/flowmaster/"premium" tips.<P>basically I just want my 2.5 to sound a little better, and free up a little horsepower.<P>TIA!<p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 03-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Eric||03-05-2001||06:25 PM||||Thanks, Travis.  I didn't know the GT had the same setup as the SE, but it sounds pretty good.  How much louder is it when cruising around?  I had an exhaust leak for a long time in my ypipe.  It got pretty loud after a while, but it never really got on my nerves at highway speeds because, like the stock system in working order, there was no resonance.  Hope the Flowmaster is the same way.||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FST2M6||03-05-2001||06:51 PM||||no the GT has a Brullen the SE has a Flowmaster. but both have 2.5" tubing and the SE has no cat.. the GT has a 2.5" catco unit.  available through <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> or <A HREF="http://www.jegs.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jegs.com</A>  (cheaper)||||reg||1
